I don't know if this is more suitable to the beginner list of the main
list, but since it's a question, I figure it may be useful to some new
folks.

Is it possible (and if so, how) to have multiple tags/connectors?

Let me explain what I mean.

On the new jboselkei (thanks for getting it back up again qx4096), I'm
trying to translate this:
"Let justice be done even as heaven falls."

And in trying to get the flavor of the "even" part of the phrase, I think
it's a kind of mixture of "ca" and ".u".  But the form "ko'a broda ko'e ca
.u ko'i" is not valid.  It's possible to mix tags like "pu ca" or "ca bai",
but I guess logical connectives are different?

